{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How It Turned Out", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Let's compare the simple past and present perfect:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span>  <br>It refers to an action that occurred at a definite time in the past.   <br><br>Examples:  <br>I said things that I didn't mean yesterday. <br>He caught me at a bad time last Saturday. <br/><br/> These actions are finished when we have a definite time (yesterday, last Saturday).<br><br>  You can use other time expressions + simple past", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He did that ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in 2000<br>                                         last night<br>                                         last weekend<br>                                         on January 2nd<br>                                          three days ago\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span><br><br>It refers to an action that happened at an indefinite time in the past.<br><br>  Examples:  <br/>You guys have always made up and moved on.<br>  I have said terrible things.<br><br>  These actions can continue to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have talked about getting married ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for years.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have been a couple ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since 2014.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have waited for Vanessa ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since she took off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never taken her suitcases.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have rather similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer.</br> However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I would always do the opposite. I would eat when I got emotional.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I used to work out when I wanted to feel refreshed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this.<br>Read the following example:<br>  <span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India.</span> (correct) <br><br>  However, when <span class=\"strong\">would</span> replaces <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, the same example becomes ungrammatical:<br><br>  <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India.</span> (not correct)<br> <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span> (correct)", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "foolishly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a foolish way; without thinking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm foolishly wasting my time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "emotional", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to someone's emotions or feelings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're not needy - you're just emotional.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "refreshed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "energized; feeling rested", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is refreshed after her travels abroad.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "reunion", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when two or more people come together after a long period of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would play our reunion over and over in my head.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to pack", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put things in a suitcase or bag for a trip", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm in my bedroom, packing my suitcase.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stubborn", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unwilling to change your mind", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're being very stubborn right now.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "anxiously", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wanting something very much", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm anxiously preparing for your visit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to await", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to wait for an event ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've anxiously awaited your visit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "study", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small room to read or study in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I keep my collection of snow globes in my study.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sincere", "type": "name"}, {"content": "honest; truthful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to show you how sincere my apology is.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob11aud10", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talk to your partner about how you deal with being emotional.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell them about what you used to do and what you do now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I talk to my partner about how I deal with being emotional.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about old and new habits.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn6le12ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn6le12ob11re2img06.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob11re2img06.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Hello?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Hi, it's me. How are you? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I've been better, but I've had time to cool off. How are you?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: I've thought about the way I acted, and I'm so sorry. You ought to break up with me, V. I'm behaving foolishly."}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob11re2img07.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "18700", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You're going to have to keep the promises that you make from now on. This is your last chance, Marco. You sound sincere.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: You mean, you've decided to come back? Oh, you've made me so happy! I'd better get your place cleaned up! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What do you mean?"}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob11re2img05.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "36000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Um, your kitchen and study are a little messy. I used to work out when I wanted to feel refreshed. Now, I cook when I get emotional.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I would always do the opposite. I would eat when I got emotional. Now, I just pack and leave. It's not a good way to handle things. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Come home and we'll have a proper reunion!  I'm anxiously awaiting your return!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: OK. I'm sorry for being so stubborn."}], "coverimg": "engenn6le12ob11re2img06.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override